::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.RS.01] Sources show a policy has benefits but needs staffing. Which synthesis is strongest?
{
~A. Staffing concerns erase all benefits.#Incorrect. This ignores part of the evidence.
=B. The policy may work when staffing needs are planned before implementation.#Correct. This connects benefit and condition.
~C. Benefits mean staffing never matters.#Incorrect. This ignores the condition.
~D. The sources cannot be connected.#Incorrect. They address the same issue.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.W.02] Which claim is strongest?
{
~A. Schools should help students.#Incorrect. This is too vague.
~B. Workshops are always perfect.#Incorrect. This overstates.
~C. Students should avoid feedback.#Incorrect. This contradicts the unit focus.
=D. Schools should provide senior transition workshops that include realistic tasks and revision after feedback.#Correct. This is specific and evidence-based.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.W.03] Which response is analysis?
{
=A. The open door functions as a symbol of revision continuing after the workshop ends.#Correct. This explains function.
~B. The passage has a room and papers.#Incorrect. This is summary.
~C. A projector is turned off.#Incorrect. This is a detail only.
~D. Students left the room.#Incorrect. This summarizes action.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Which paraphrase preserves meaning: "Students revised materials after feedback"?
{
~A. Students ignored all feedback.#Incorrect. This reverses meaning.
~B. Students never revised.#Incorrect. This contradicts the source.
=C. Students improved their materials after receiving responses.#Correct. This preserves meaning.
~D. Students only took a test.#Incorrect. This changes the source.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Which revision improves vague writing?
{
~A. Repeat "good" several times.#Incorrect. Repetition does not improve writing.
~B. Remove all evidence.#Incorrect. Evidence is needed.
=C. Replace "good sources" with "sources that show realistic practice and revision improve preparation."#Correct. This adds precision.
~D. Use slang instead of explanation.#Incorrect. Academic writing needs clarity.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q06::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Which sentence is clearest?
{
=A. Workshops can support seniors when they include examples, feedback, and revision time.#Correct. This is clear and complete.
~B. Because workshops and students revision.#Incorrect. This is fragmented.
~C. Students things later.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~D. Revision, examples, because.#Incorrect. This is incomplete.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q07::[MLA.ENG4.W.02] Which communication choice fits an academic checkpoint?
{
~A. Use no evidence and informal slang.#Incorrect. This does not fit the audience.
~B. Submit a blank response.#Incorrect. This does not show mastery.
~C. Hide the main point.#Incorrect. Clear communication states the point.
=D. State a clear claim, use evidence, and explain reasoning professionally.#Correct. This matches academic communication.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q08::[MLA.ENG4.R.06] Which structure best supports argument development?
{
~A. Random detail, title, unrelated fact.#Incorrect. This is not logical.
=B. Claim, evidence, elaboration, consequence.#Correct. This order supports clear development.
~C. Evidence only with no explanation.#Incorrect. Evidence needs elaboration.
~D. Conclusion before any claim or evidence.#Incorrect. This can confuse readers.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q09::[MLA.ENG4.R.12] A workplace communication argument connects to which broader concern?
{
~A. Font size only.#Incorrect. This is not a broad concern.
~B. Avoiding all revision.#Incorrect. Revision matters.
=C. Audience awareness and responsibility beyond school.#Correct. This is a broader concern.
~D. Ignoring purpose.#Incorrect. Purpose matters.
}

::ENG4_U04_PRE_Q10::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Which word means the job a detail performs in a text?
{
=A. Function#Correct. Function means the job a choice performs.
~B. Guess#Incorrect. Analysis should not rely on guessing.
~C. Copy#Incorrect. Copying is not function.
~D. Error#Incorrect. Error does not mean function.
}
